      <title>‘The doom of humanity’: will the quest to make robotic hands render us obsolete?</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/21/robot-hands-future-of-humanity-ai</link>
      <description>The one thing stopping AI taking over the world – or at least everyone’s jobs? Dexterity. Human hands are anatomical marvels that engineers have struggled for years to replicate. Experts are racing to change that Just outside Luton, in an Amazon warehouse the size of four football pitches, yellow shelving units pirouette in a digitally choreographed dance. Tubs containing a Lego Spider-Man kit, followed by dishwasher tablets, followed by a pouch of muscle building protein powder whiz along…</description>
